{"gid":"026f5843-b6af-4777-a7c2-d9f5c280134b","runId":"mockgen-20260929","skill":"equivalent_expressions","domain":"advanced_math","examSystem":"sat_math","difficulty":"medium","format":"spr","problem":{"format":"spr","figure":null,"passage":"The expression $\\dfrac{6x^2 - 13x - 5}{2x - 5}$ is equivalent to $ax + b$, where $a$ and $b$ are constants, for all values of $x$ for which the original expression is defined.\n\nWhat is the value of $a + b$?","stimulus":"The expression $\\dfrac{6x^2 - 13x - 5}{2x - 5}$ is equivalent to $ax + b$, where $a$ and $b$ are constants, for all values of $x$ for which the original expression is defined.","question":"What is the value of $a + b$?","needsFigure":false,"options":null,"correctIndex":null,"answers":["4"],"statements":null,"explanation":"분자 $6x^2-13x-5$를 인수분해하면 $(2x-5)(3x+1)$이 됨을 확인한다. $6x^2-13x-5 = 6x^2 -15x +2x -5 = 3x(2x-5)+1(2x-5) = (2x-5)(3x+1)$. 따라서 $\\dfrac{6x^2-13x-5}{2x-5} = \\dfrac{(2x-5)(3x+1)}{2x-5} = 3x+1$ ($x \\neq 5/2$). 그러므로 $a=3$, $b=1$이고 $a+b=4$이다.","explanationEn":"Factor the numerator $6x^2-13x-5$ as $(2x-5)(3x+1)$: check that $6x^2-13x-5 = 6x^2-15x+2x-5 = 3x(2x-5)+1(2x-5) = (2x-5)(3x+1)$. Then $\\dfrac{6x^2-13x-5}{2x-5} = \\dfrac{(2x-5)(3x+1)}{2x-5} = 3x+1$ for $x \\neq 5/2$. So $a=3$, $b=1$, and $a+b=4$.","difficulty":"medium","distractorRationales":[],"difficultyRationale":"","design":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null},"quality":{"contract":{"ok":true,"issues":[]},"estimatedDifficulty":"medium","requestedDifficulty":"medium","difficultyReasons":["다항식을 인수분해하거나 나눗셈을 수행해야 함 (2단계)","6x^2-13x-5를 (2x-5)(3x+1)로 인수분해하는 과정에서 부호 실수가 생기기 쉬움","a,b를 구한 뒤 합을 구하는 마지막 단계까지 정확히 수행해야 함"],"distractors":[],"independentReview":{"pickedIndex":null,"pickedAnswer":"4","agrees":true,"confidence":"high","flags":[]},"needsReview":false,"needsReviewReasons":[],"calibrated":false,"reviewedAt":"2026-09-30T06:21:17.952Z"},"generatedAt":"2026-09-30T06:21:17.952Z"}